+`refreshing` on a transient error moves to `retrying` while fewer than two retries were made, else to `failed`. The backoff delays are the spec's (500 ms before the first retry, 2 s before the second; `specs/session-refresh/spec.md`). `refresh()` waits through an injected `sleep(ms)` dependency, defaulting to a `setTimeout` wrapper, and never reads the wall clock itself. Tests pass a fake `sleep` that records each requested delay and resolves at once, so the delays are asserted exactly, whatever the machine's speed.
 
 ## Verification
 
 F1 scenario 2 (shared in-flight refresh) keeps its outputs under `f1/scenario-2/`.
+
+F1 runs the shipped desktop client build unmodified. Only its IdP endpoint setting points at the local fixture `tools/fake-idp.ts`. The fixture is a disposable verification helper. It answers the client's real token-endpoint requests with the provider's response shapes: HTTP 503, HTTP 400 with body `{"error":"invalid_grant"}`, and HTTP 200 with a token JSON body. All retry, state and single-flight logic under test is therefore the code that ships, and only the IdP's answers are scripted.
